Combating Alert Fatigue with NVD-Grounded Context
A Tier 1 security analyst is tasked with reviewing daily reports from a traditional Static Application Security Testing (SAST) tool. 
The legacy tool relies on rigid regular expressions and flags thousands of potential issues with no context, causing severe alert fatigue. 
Instead of manually researching every alert, the analyst feeds the suspicious code snippets into your scanner. 
The RAG pipeline cross-references the code directly against the local NIST NVD database, filtering out false positives 
and prioritizing only the vulnerabilities that map to real, documented CVEs.
